        "subject": "DRAFT  LU-xxxxx lod: add standalone kunit test for RR/QoS stripe allocators",
        "message": "DRAFT  LU-xxxxx lod: add standalone kunit test for RR/QoS stripe allocators\n\nAdd lustre/kunit/lod_alloc_test.c, a standalone kunit module that\nexercises lod_ost_alloc_rr() and lod_ost_alloc_qos() directly against\na loaded lod.ko, without mounting a Lustre filesystem or going through\nlod_comp_prep_create()/lod_prepare_create(). It builds a minimal\nlod_device and a set of fake OSTs (fake dt_device + obd_export +\nlu_tgt_desc) by hand, and verifies that each allocator, when every OST\nis healthy and overstriping is not requested, allocates exactly the\nrequested number of stripes using distinct, valid OST indices -- up to\nand including using every OST in the pool.\n\nThis deliberately only tests the allocators in isolation: EC\ndata/parity pairing and FLR mirror allocation live one layer up in\nlod_comp_prep_create() and will need a separate kunit module driving\nthat entry point.\n\nTo make this possible:\n- De-staticize and export lod_ost_alloc_rr() and lod_ost_alloc_qos(),\n  and export lod_lu_ops and lod_thread_key, so the test module can\n  call into the allocators and build a usable lod_device/lu_env.\n- Add a KUNIT_STATIC_STUB_REDIRECT() to lod_qos_declare_object_on(),\n  so a kunit test can replace it with a fake dt_object, since the real\n  path requires a live OSD/OSP under each OST.\n- Add a timer_container_of() compat fallback in\n  lustre_compat/linux/timer.h for older kernels that don't provide it.\n\nThe test module is a real kunit_test_suite(), reporting results via\nnative KTAP output, and is wired into lustre/kunit/Makefile under\nCONFIG_LUSTRE_FS_SERVER alongside the other kunit test modules.\n\nChange-Id: Ide36025d81afedf202c94f15fb24722dd7134686\nSigned-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <rsahlberg@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master",
      "description": "Edit commit message"
    }
